
# gantry-axis Cyclic Synchronous mode flow:

## Startup
1. No SYNC on startup
2. If switch to Cyclic mode:
  1. If (cyclic mode different than previous mode) {
    1. For Each drive:
      1. Set NMT to PRE-OP
      2. Configure required params for this new cyclic mode (see below)
      // This is optional? Would require PDO parsing to know current mode
      3. Configure minimal PDO mapping specific to this cyclic mode 
      4. Set NMT to OP
      5. Start SYNC producer, Send cyclic mode target (eg 6071h for torque) every cycle
      6. Set Cia402 to OPERATION ENABLED
  }
  2. loop:
    1. Send SYNC
    // Note: in cyclic torque (and vel? pos?) mode we could do X axis Synchronosation here
    2. Send new cyclic target to all drives

## Switch to non-cyclic mode
1. If switch to non-cyclic mode:
  1. For Each Drive:
    1. Switch back to default PDO mapping
    2. Switch into new mode
    3. Stop SYNC generation

  loop:
  2. Start passing new setpoints to each drive

# Required params per cyclic mode
## Position
datasheet 6.7.2
## Velocity
datasheet 6.8.2
## Torque
datasheet 6.9.2
  
